TIP:  Single strums for chords in the verse.

Tip:  TIP:  There's one lonely (B) after the 2nd chorus on "say".  It will follow an (A) so play that (A) with your lower 3 fingers and slide up to the 3rd fret to play the (B).

TIP:  The vocal transition between the first chorus and the 2nd verse can be a bit tricky.  You end the chorus on a downward inflection on note <a>, open 5th string of the |Am|.  For the next line (first line of the second verse) you stay on that note but walk up so the next (Am) comes on note <e>, covered 4th string of the (Am).
    

